# Parameter passing

Default recommendations for **new and touched** APIs. Not a mandate to mass-rewrite stable public surfaces.

## Quick table

| Case | Prefer | Avoid |
|------|--------|--------|
| Scalars, enums, raw pointers | by value `T` | needless `const int&` |
| Large read-only (STL containers, big structs) | `const T&` | accidental deep copy by value |
| New **parse/match** string APIs | `QStringView` / `std::string_view` **by value** | `const QStringView&`; storing views in members without lifetime proof |
| Sync Qt COW read-only (`QString`, `QByteArray`, …) | `const T&` is fine | forced whole-repo `QStringView` churn |
| Sink / store into member (ctors, take-ownership helpers) | `QString` / `std::string` **by value** + `std::move` | `const QString&` then copy into member when a sink is clearer |
| Mutate caller's object | `T&` | out-params that are never null disguised as pointers |
| `QObject` / `QWidget` | `T*` (null-check if allowed) | by-value; don't invent `shared_ptr<QWidget>` without real shared ownership |
| Exclusive ownership handoff | `std::unique_ptr<T>` by value | naked `new` with unclear deleter |
| Shared long-term hold | `std::shared_ptr<T>` by value | by-value `shared_ptr` on hot read-only observe paths → prefer `T*` / `const shared_ptr&` |
| Queued / cross-thread signals | copyable args or `shared_ptr` for big payloads | non-const `T&` "out" params |

## Hard rules (correctness)

1. Never pass `QObject` by value.
2. Do not store `QStringView` / `string_view` in members unless the buffer outlives the object.
3. Cross-thread signal parameters must be meta-type friendly; no non-const reference mutation across threads.
4. When reviewing, prioritize **correctness / lifetime / cross-thread copies** over style nits.

## Do not

- Convert every `const QString&` setter to `QStringView` "for modernity".
- Treat `const int&` → `int` as a merge-blocking fix outside hot paths.
- Rewrite sink ctors that already take `QString` by value into `const QString&`.

## Review output (when asked)

1. Findings with severity (correctness > lifetime > cross-thread > style).
2. Suggested signatures only.
3. Explicitly list items left alone and why.
